 ### [Differential Data Stream (DDS) File Format](1754-differential-data-stream-dds-file-format.md)
-The Differential Data Stream (DDS) file format is a lossless compression method for volume data that encodes differential values using run-length encoding and adaptive bit allocation per run. It is designed to handle multi-channel volume data by interleaving channels and applying spatial/temporal differencing, making it distinct from transform-based methods like [Triadic frequency band decomposition](828-triadic-frequency-band-decomposition.md) or [Laplacian Pyramid](2250-laplacian-pyramid.md) by operating directly on raw pixel/voxel values without frequency decomposition. It builds on [Value compression](6-value-compression.md) principles by focusing on the statistical redundancy of differences between adjacent voxels.
