-Predictive and Differential Coding reduces volumetric data redundancy by encoding the difference (residual) between a voxel's actual value and a predicted value derived from its neighbors or reference frames, rather than encoding the absolute values. It sets itself apart from transform-based methods (like [Wavelet and Transform-based Compression](52-wavelet-and-transform-based-compression.md)) by operating directly on spatial or temporal dependencies without requiring a global frequency decomposition, making it highly effective for data with strong local coherence.
