 ### [Burrows-Wheeler Transform](6541-burrows-wheeler-transform.md)
-The Burrows-Wheeler Transform (BWT) is a reversible permutation scheme that re-sorts a block of data according to its local context, organizing it into a form that is highly compressible for subsequent entropy coding. Unlike the linear decorrelation transforms in its family (such as Wavelets or KLT), BWT does not change the data values but rearranges their positions to group identical or similar symbols together, thereby increasing redundancy. It is distinguished by its ability to create long runs of identical characters, which are efficiently handled by Run-Length Encoding (RLE) or Move-to-Front (MTF) transforms before entropy coding.
